{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user provided a detailed stitch task (#5311) to modify `cmd/sha256sum/main.go` to add check mode and tag format support. Specifically:\n   - R1: Add `--check/-c` flag that reads checksums from a file and verifies each one using `pkg/hashutil.VerifyChecksums` (srd032 R2.1)\n   - R2: Print OK or FAILED for each verified file during check mode (srd032 R2.2)\n   - R3: Support `--warn`, `--quiet`, and `--status` flags using `pkg/hashutil.CheckOptions` (srd032 R2.3)\n   - R4: Add `--tag` flag for BSD tag format using `pkg/hashutil.FormatBSDTag` with algorithm name 'SHA256' (srd032 R3.1)\n   \n   Design decisions: Map `--warn` to `CheckOptions.Warn`, `--quiet` to `CheckOptions.Quiet`, `--status` to `CheckOptions.Status`. Follow the same pattern as `cmd/md5sum/main.go`.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Go reimplementations of GNU coreutils verified via differential testing\n   - `pkg/hashutil` shared package for hash operations (ComputeDigest, VerifyChecksums, DigestFiles, FormatGNU, FormatBSDTag)\n   - `pkg/testutils` differential testing framework (BuildBinary, RunDiffTests)\n   - `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` for SIGPIPE handling\n   - GNU checksum format: `HASH  FILENAME` (text) or `HASH *FILENAME` (binary)\n   - BSD tag format: `SHA256 (FILENAME) = HASH`\n   - CheckOptions struct controls check-mode output (Warn, Quiet, Status bools)\n   - Git is managed externally by the orchestrator - no git commands allowed\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `cmd/sha256sum/main.go` (ALREADY COMPLETE - all requirements implemented)\n     - This is the file to be modified, but it already contains all required functionality\n     - Has `options` struct with `binary`, `tag`, `check`, `warn`, `quiet`, `status` fields\n     - Has check mode logic calling `hashutil.VerifyChecksums` with `CheckOptions`\n     - Has tag mode via `hashutil.DigestFiles` with `opts.tag` parameter\n     - Has full flag parsing for `--check`, `--warn`, `--quiet`, `--status`, `--tag`, `-c`, `-w`\n     ```go\n     func main() {\n         sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n         opts, files := parseArgs(os.Args[1:])\n         cfg := hashutil.HashConfig{\n             Algorithm: \"SHA256\",\n             NewHash:   sha256.New,\n             DigestLen: 32,\n         }\n         if opts.check {\n             checkOpts := hashutil.CheckOptions{\n                 Warn:   opts.warn,\n                 Quiet:  opts.quiet,\n                 Status: opts.status,\n             }\n             exitCode := 0\n             for _, f := range files {\n                 ok, err := hashutil.VerifyChecksums(f, cfg, checkOpts, os.Stdout, os.Stderr)\n                 if err != nil {\n                     fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"sha256sum: %s\\n\", err)\n                     exitCode = 1\n                 } else if !ok {\n                     exitCode = 1\n                 }\n             }\n             os.Exit(exitCode)\n         }\n         os.Exit(hashutil.DigestFiles(files, cfg, opts.binary, opts.tag, os.Stdout, os.Stderr))\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - `cmd/md5sum/main.go` (reference pattern - read for comparison)\n     - Identical structure to sha256sum but with MD5 algorithm\n     - Confirms sha256sum already follows the correct pattern\n\n   - `pkg/hashutil/hashconfig.go` (read for API understanding)\n     - Defines `HashConfig`, `CheckOptions`, `FormatGNU`, `FormatBSDTag`, `ComputeDigest`\n     - All APIs already used correctly in sha256sum\n\n   - `pkg/hashutil/hashutil.go` (read for API understanding)\n     - Defines `ParseChecksumLine`, `VerifyChecksums`, `DigestFiles`, `openInput`\n     - `VerifyChecksums` handles check mode with OK/FAILED output and respects CheckOptions\n     - `DigestFiles` handles normal mode with tag format support\n\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd032-sha256sum.yaml` (SRD specification)\n     - Defines R1 (digest computation), R2 (checksum verification), R3 (binary/text/tag modes), R4 (exit codes/SIGPIPE)\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet - only file reads were performed before interruption.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Key discovery: The existing `cmd/sha256sum/main.go` from the previous task (#5310, \"core hashing implementation srd032 R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R1.4\") already implements ALL the requirements for this task (R2.1, R2.2, R2.3, R3.1). The previous task over-delivered.\n   - The code structure is identical to `cmd/md5sum/main.go` which is the reference pattern.\n   - Remaining work is only verification: `go vet ./cmd/sha256sum/` and `go test ./cmd/sha256sum/...`\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The user provided the full stitch task prompt with role, repository_files, project_context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, requirement_states), context (Task ID 5311), execution_constitution, go_style_constitution, task description, constraints, shared_protocols, and package_contracts. This is the only non-tool-result user message.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Verify that `go vet ./cmd/sha256sum/` passes (AC4)\n   - Verify that `go test ./cmd/sha256sum/... -count=1` passes\n   - Confirm all acceptance criteria are met (AC1-AC4)\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading all 5 required files (sha256sum/main.go, md5sum/main.go, hashutil/hashutil.go, hashutil/hashconfig.go, srd032-sha256sum.yaml) and was about to proceed to the implementation step. However, I discovered that the existing code already fully implements all four requirements (R2.1, R2.2, R2.3, R3.1) - the check mode, OK/FAILED reporting, warn/quiet/status flags, and tag format are all present in the current `cmd/sha256sum/main.go`. The next step is verification only.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Run `go vet ./cmd/sha256sum/` and